.TITLE2{present - `templates`}

```txt
#dot#template{TITLE}
#dot#header
#dot#div{margin-left: 3svw;}(##  {{.}})
<hr>
#dot#header.end
#dot#footer
#dot#div{position: absolute; left: 91svw;}(#dot#image(icon.png 8svw:))
#dot#footer.end
```
.================================
.TITLE2{present - `templates with arguments`}

```txt
#dot#template{FROM_TO}(From,To)
{{.From}}:{{.To}})
#dot#template.end
```
```txt
.FROM_TO{From}(10){To}(20)
```
.================================
.TITLE2{present - code}

- editable
- inline or imported from file
- run in `tmp` or in specific folder
- partially shown (with edit option)
- response seen in presentation in terminal

.================================
.TITLE2{present - code}

```txt
#dot#cast.edit.save(main.go).run(go run .).before(go mod init x)
```

#space#
.cast.edit.save(main.go).run(go run .).before(go mod init x)
```go
package main

import (
	"fmt"
)

func main() {
	fmt.Println("hello DORS/CLUC 30")
}
```

.================================
.TITLE2{present - code}

```txt
#dot#cast.stream.edit.save(main.go).run(go run .).show(9:11)
```

#space#
  .cast.stream.edit.save(main.go).run(go run .).before(go mod init x).show(9:11)
```go
package main

import (
  "fmt"
  "time"
)

func main() {
  fmt.Println("hello")
  time.Sleep(3 * time.Second)
  fmt.Println("world")
}
```

